TESTSUITE "DYNCALL dynamic call boundaries"

*> One MOCK CALL <identifier> directive (bare key = dynamic CALL) matches
*> every CALL through WS-PGM-NAME, including the nested one inside the IF.
*> The mock body branches on the identifier's runtime value -- per-target
*> behavior without any runtime program resolution: the splicer replaced
*> the whole CALL statement, so nothing is ever really called.
TESTCASE "one identifier mock dispatches on the runtime target"
    MOCK CALL WS-PGM-NAME
        IF WS-PGM-NAME = "PGMA"
            MOVE 1 TO WS-RC
        ELSE
            MOVE 2 TO WS-RC
        END-IF
    END-MOCK
    PERFORM MAIN-PROCESS
    EXPECT WS-TOTAL TO BE 5
    VERIFY CALL WS-PGM-NAME WAS CALLED 3 TIMES
